1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,740
Hello again!

2
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:04,500
Last time, I said the family works the other way round.

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:08,080
Today, we learn the family trick for taking away.

4
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:10,020
But first, a puzzle.

5
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:12,360
Eleven take away six.

6
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,220
Make eleven.

7
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:19,220
One lower bead on the ones rod, and one lower bead on the tens rod.

8
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,220
Thumb pushes them up.

9
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,520
Six's friend is four.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,560
The big friend says: add four to the ones rod, then take ten off the tens rod.

11
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:30,800
Quick guess.

12
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:34,340
Is there room for four more lower beads on the ones rod?

13
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:36,840
Nope!

14
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,300
Only three fit.

15
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:39,520
Whoa.

16
00:00:39,820 --> 00:00:41,160
The big friend is stuck.

17
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:42,640
Why?

18
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:47,100
The upper bead is up, and the lower beads are almost full.

19
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:48,980
No room to add four.

20
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:50,340
Who can help?

21
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:53,380
The small friend!

22
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,640
Four's small friend is one.

23
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,620
To add four: take away one, then add five.

24
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:03,100
The big friend and the small friend, side by side.

25
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,360
That team is called the family.

26
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,380
Here is our routine.

27
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:08,100
Look.

28
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:09,040
Call.

29
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:09,800
Move.

30
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,500
Look: room on the ones rod?

31
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:15,760
Call: no room, call the family.

32
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,140
Move: ones rod first.

33
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:23,940
The big friend says: minus six equals plus four, minus ten.

34
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:28,760
The small friend swaps plus four for minus one, plus five.

35
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:35,000
So the family says: minus six equals minus one, plus five, minus ten.

36
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:37,520
Why?

37
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,320
Minus ten takes four too many.

38
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,540
So we add four back first.

39
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,080
Now remember last time.

40
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,840
Plus six was plus one, minus five, plus ten.

41
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:50,420
What changed today?

42
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,820
Every sign flipped!

43
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,000
It is a mirror.

44
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:58,240
So which finger now, thumb or index?

45
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,500
Index finger!

46
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:03,000
Adding went up.

47
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,960
Taking away goes down.

48
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:06,540
Up is the thumb.

49
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,280
Down is the index finger.

50
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:10,440
Move.

51
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,400
Lower beads first, then the upper bead.

52
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,680
Minus one.

53
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,600
The lower bead goes down.

54
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,180
Plus five.

55
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:20,080
The upper bead goes down.

56
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,820
Tens rod last.

57
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,640
One bead goes down.

58
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:24,700
Boom!

59
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,400
Eleven take away six is five.

60
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:32,020
Next: twenty-two take away seven.

61
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,060
Make it.

62
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:37,920
Two lower beads on the ones rod, and two lower beads on the tens rod.

63
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:38,900
Thumb up!

64
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:40,120
Look.

65
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:42,000
Seven's friend is three.

66
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,980
Room for three more lower beads?

67
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:46,700
No!

68
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,040
Just two fit.

69
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:49,000
Call.

70
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:53,460
Minus seven equals minus two, plus five, minus ten.

71
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:55,900
Move.

72
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,240
Minus two.

73
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:59,080
Two lower beads go down.

74
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:00,780
Now plus five.

75
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:02,120
Upper bead down.

76
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:03,660
Tens rod.

77
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:05,400
One bead goes down.

78
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:07,400
Index finger, every time!

79
00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:08,180
Boom!

80
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,720
Twenty-two take away seven is fifteen!

81
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,960
Mirror fans, tap like!

82
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:16,760
And subscribe, the next trick is a big one.

83
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:17,920
Minus eight.

84
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:19,300
Make ninety-three.

85
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:22,200
On the ones rod, three lower beads.

86
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:26,380
Then on the tens rod, four lower beads and the upper bead.

87
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:30,040
Thumb for the lower beads, index finger for the upper bead.

88
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:30,900
Look.

89
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:32,840
Eight's friend is two.

90
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,960
How many more lower beads fit?

91
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:37,860
Only one!

92
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:38,560
Call.

93
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,820
Minus eight equals minus three, plus five, minus ten.

94
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:44,360
Move.

95
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:45,680
Minus three.

96
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,580
Three lower beads go down.

97
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:49,620
Then plus five.

98
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,400
Down goes the upper bead.

99
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:52,900
Tens rod.

100
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:54,440
One bead goes down.

101
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:55,240
Boom!

102
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:58,000
Ninety-three take away eight is eighty-five!

103
00:03:59,280 --> 00:03:59,760
Flip it.

104
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,140
Plus family: up, thumb.

105
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:05,300
Minus family: down, index finger.

106
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:10,180
Plus family: plus lower beads, minus five, plus ten.

107
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:15,180
Minus family: minus lower beads, plus five, minus ten.

108
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,480
Same numbers.

109
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:17,740
Mirror moves.

110
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:23,420
Minus six, minus seven, minus eight, minus nine.

111
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:25,060
Four mirror formulas.

112
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:26,420
Your go.

113
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:27,680
Make eighty-four.

114
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,260
On the ones rod, four lower beads.

115
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:34,120
Then on the tens rod, three lower beads and the upper bead.

116
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:35,180
Choose your fingers!

117
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:36,480
Look.

118
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,220
What is nine's friend?

119
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:40,300
One!

120
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:41,760
Check the ones rod.

121
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,240
Four lower beads already.

122
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:44,720
No room at all!

123
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:45,560
Call.

124
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:48,020
Nine is five and four more.

125
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:50,300
So how many lower beads come off first?

126
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:52,380
Four!

127
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:56,540
Minus nine equals minus four, plus five, minus ten.

128
00:04:57,780 --> 00:04:57,860
Move.

129
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,440
All down, so all index finger.

130
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:01,760
Ones rod first.

131
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,300
What number is showing now?

132
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,440
Eighty-four take away nine is seventy-five!

133
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:09,920
Mirror master!

134
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:13,260
You did Look, Call, Move all by yourself.

135
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,540
Try Look, Call, Move on your own abacus.

136
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:20,080
Get Abacus Kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

137
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,040
It is free.

138
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,154
Next time, we play a family game.

139
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:26,240
Can you find the missing step?

140
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:27,000
See you next time!
